00:00:00.345 --> 00:00:01.778
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.778 --> 00:00:04.661
Today's message is start small.

00:00:04.661 --> 00:00:06.344
Over to you, John Williams.

00:00:06.344 --> 00:00:08.161
(rooster cawing)

00:00:08.161 --> 00:00:11.451
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.451 --> 00:00:14.016
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.016 --> 00:00:17.926
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:20.018
- First work that I did in
the Hollywood Film Studios

00:00:20.018 --> 00:00:21.435
was as a pianist.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.982
In the old Columbia Studios

00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:27.252
where they had a contract orchestra,

00:00:27.252 --> 00:00:29.226
there was an opening position for piano

00:00:29.226 --> 00:00:30.059
which I auditioned for,

00:00:30.059 --> 00:00:32.716
and I was hired by the then
music director Morris Stoloff,

00:00:32.716 --> 00:00:35.148
who the young people will not remember.

00:00:35.148 --> 00:00:38.671
So, that meant that every
day, Monday through Friday,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.457
four or five days a week,

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:42.708
I sat in the orchestra at Columbia Studios

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:45.738
playing under Mr. Stoloff's direction

00:00:45.738 --> 00:00:49.558
and watching him underscore
films about westerns

00:00:49.558 --> 00:00:53.725
or love stories or scary
films or comedies or whatever

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.924
and had a first hand view
as an orchestra member

00:00:58.924 --> 00:01:01.268
of how this process of creating

00:01:01.268 --> 00:01:04.613
and fitting music to film went,

00:01:04.613 --> 00:01:07.708
and two or three years into my
time in the orchestra there,

00:01:07.708 --> 00:01:11.033
the same gentleman said,
"Would you prepare the music

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:14.632
"for one scene for next week's recording?"

00:01:14.632 --> 00:01:16.917
So I did one scene for
next week's recording

00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:19.225
and apparently worked out well enough

00:01:19.225 --> 00:01:22.323
that he said in two weeks,
"Would you do two scenes for us?

00:01:22.323 --> 00:01:25.176
"We're a little short this
week, maybe three a week later."

00:01:25.176 --> 00:01:29.765
So it was a series of steps or
increments if you like to say

00:01:29.765 --> 00:01:32.039
I progressed from the piano bench

00:01:32.039 --> 00:01:34.481
of sitting in the orchestra
and playing the piano

00:01:34.481 --> 00:01:37.262
to a young man sitting not
far from the music library

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:40.011
writing the music for
next Tuesday's recording.

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:41.447
- I think it's really
important for entrepreneurs

00:01:41.447 --> 00:01:44.678
that you have a big
vision but start small.

00:01:44.678 --> 00:01:48.855
You have a big vision but you start small.

00:01:48.855 --> 00:01:52.588
And a lot of entrepreneurs
have a hard time doing this.

00:01:52.588 --> 00:01:54.053
You've got the two types of people,

00:01:54.053 --> 00:01:56.647
the first are the people who think big

00:01:56.647 --> 00:01:58.625
and only want to act big.

00:01:58.625 --> 00:01:59.789
You're the dreamers,

00:01:59.789 --> 00:02:01.251
you're the non-conformists,

00:02:01.251 --> 00:02:02.624
you have this big vision

00:02:02.624 --> 00:02:03.950
for how you want to change the world

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.509
and what your role in it is going to be,

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:07.169
how you're going to be the next Steve Jobs

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:09.984
and take a dent out of the universe.

00:02:09.984 --> 00:02:13.621
I love it but you have
to do something, right?

00:02:13.621 --> 00:02:16.674
And so many of those entrepreneurs
just have these ideas

00:02:16.674 --> 00:02:17.554
and then they get frustrated

00:02:17.554 --> 00:02:19.080
'cause they never get their big break

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.657
because they don't want
to take small steps,

00:02:20.657 --> 00:02:22.656
they want to take giant leaps forward

00:02:22.656 --> 00:02:24.413
where you need to understand

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:26.207
that to take the giant leap forward

00:02:26.207 --> 00:02:28.469
you have to start with the smallest step.

00:02:28.469 --> 00:02:31.037
And a lot of times people see
that as being beneath them.

00:02:31.037 --> 00:02:32.609
Well, I don't want to do
that little tiny thing,

00:02:32.609 --> 00:02:34.586
I'm a big dreamer, I'm a visionary,

00:02:34.586 --> 00:02:36.465
I want to take huge, giant steps.

00:02:36.465 --> 00:02:38.437
But doing nothing,

00:02:38.437 --> 00:02:40.944
which was what most of
these visionaries do,

00:02:40.944 --> 00:02:42.912
they do nothing, just sit on your idea,

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:45.484
never gets you to that big, giant step.

00:02:45.484 --> 00:02:48.906
You've got to take
small, consistent actions

00:02:48.906 --> 00:02:51.560
and what that does is
helps you get better,

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.081
it helps you learn the market more,

00:02:53.081 --> 00:02:54.099
it helps you improve your skills,

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:56.365
it helps you improve your connections,

00:02:56.365 --> 00:02:58.156
helps you create more value.

00:02:58.156 --> 00:03:01.124
And then that small step becomes
a slightly less small step

00:03:01.124 --> 00:03:02.969
and becomes this even
slightly less small step

00:03:02.969 --> 00:03:04.993
and you get bigger and
bigger and bigger and bigger.

00:03:04.993 --> 00:03:06.689
And if you do that consistently,

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:07.522
you'll look back and say,

00:03:07.522 --> 00:03:09.852
"Wow, I took this giant leap forward."

00:03:09.852 --> 00:03:12.298
And people will say you
became this overnight success

00:03:12.298 --> 00:03:15.557
but really it's because of
years of taking small steps

00:03:15.557 --> 00:03:16.409
and slowly making those

00:03:16.409 --> 00:03:18.011
bigger and bigger and bigger and bigger.

00:03:18.011 --> 00:03:19.044
So you need to act.

00:03:19.044 --> 00:03:20.788
I love the big visionary thinking,

00:03:20.788 --> 00:03:22.011
I absolutely love it.

00:03:22.011 --> 00:03:23.344
You're going to take over the world,

00:03:23.344 --> 00:03:26.709
have a huge impact, solve
a major problem, I love it

00:03:26.709 --> 00:03:28.323
but you have to do something.

00:03:28.323 --> 00:03:29.548
Start small.

00:03:29.548 --> 00:03:31.452
You want to be the next huge YouTuber,

00:03:31.452 --> 00:03:34.288
I love it, amazing, but
you're not going to start

00:03:34.288 --> 00:03:36.428
until you get the gear and the lighting

00:03:36.428 --> 00:03:39.455
and the microphone and the
set up and all of that.

00:03:39.455 --> 00:03:41.670
You're not going to start
till you have an editor

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:42.985
and a producer and all this stuff.

00:03:42.985 --> 00:03:43.987
You're not going to get that.

00:03:43.987 --> 00:03:45.593
Nobody's going to give that to you.

00:03:45.593 --> 00:03:47.045
And if you had it, you would suck

00:03:47.045 --> 00:03:48.980
'cause you have no experience or practice.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.685
So it's okay to take out your phone

00:03:50.685 --> 00:03:51.757
and start recording like that.

00:03:51.757 --> 00:03:54.684
Start, take action, get better.

00:03:54.684 --> 00:03:57.669
And those small steps will
lead to the bigger and bigger

00:03:57.669 --> 00:03:59.594
and bigger and bigger steps.

00:03:59.594 --> 00:04:01.122
It's so important.

00:04:01.122 --> 00:04:02.346
So many of you are just
lost in your dreams

00:04:02.346 --> 00:04:03.353
that you don't do anything.

00:04:03.353 --> 00:04:05.043
You've got to do something.

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:06.985
Then there's the other entrepreneurs,

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:11.281
who start small but then
they also think small.

00:04:11.281 --> 00:04:12.769
There is no bigger vision.

00:04:12.769 --> 00:04:14.510
They stay stuck where they are.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.231
And maybe that's a part time income,

00:04:16.231 --> 00:04:17.880
maybe that's even a full time income,

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:18.903
maybe that's even the point

00:04:18.903 --> 00:04:20.610
where you've built up to the point

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.010
where you can provide opportunities

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.142
for other people as well.

00:04:23.142 --> 00:04:26.794
You've got a team but your
vision is still limited.

00:04:26.794 --> 00:04:29.585
Those people could push to think bigger,

00:04:29.585 --> 00:04:31.275
to have a greater impact.

00:04:31.275 --> 00:04:32.900
You're great at executing

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.343
but you're not great at pushing harder

00:04:35.343 --> 00:04:38.246
'cause you're stuck in always
trying to be practical mode.

00:04:38.246 --> 00:04:39.692
And so there aren't
that many entrepreneurs

00:04:39.692 --> 00:04:41.698
that are a good balance of both

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:43.390
where you have the big vision

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.727
but you're willing to grind it out

00:04:44.727 --> 00:04:46.334
and do all the small steps.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:48.939
And so whatever category you fall into,

00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:52.190
you could learn from
going to the other side.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.444
The visionary needs to
learn from the hustler

00:04:54.444 --> 00:04:56.593
who will grind out every little small step

00:04:56.593 --> 00:04:58.792
and that grinder, hustler
could learn from the visionary

00:04:58.792 --> 00:05:01.186
in thinking bigger how
to explode their company.

00:05:01.186 --> 00:05:02.944
And so the question of the day today is

00:05:02.944 --> 00:05:04.891
I'm curious, I want to know from you,

00:05:04.891 --> 00:05:07.847
your big vision, number
one, what your big vision is

00:05:07.847 --> 00:05:12.491
and two, what the small step
you're going to do today is

00:05:12.491 --> 00:05:15.772
to build that business a
little bit further forward.

00:05:15.772 --> 00:05:16.921
Leave it in the comments below.

00:05:16.921 --> 00:05:18.385
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:05:18.385 --> 00:05:20.929
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Omar Karamat.

