00:05:53.257 --> 00:05:55.543
- Best way to establish
yourself on the internet

00:05:55.543 --> 00:05:59.432
is to start small, once again, be humble,

00:05:59.432 --> 00:06:00.667
approach one of these blogs,

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:02.072
first of all, you got to make
sure your music is correct

00:06:02.072 --> 00:06:04.745
'cause there's a million
niggas online doing music

00:06:04.745 --> 00:06:07.701
but once you feel like your
music is truly correct,

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.419
stay humble, start small,

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:11.200
go to like some of the smaller blogs

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.650
that they don't get as
many hits as the NahRights

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:16.399
but maybe they'll post
your shit if they like it.

00:06:16.399 --> 00:06:20.162
You know, shout out to DC to
BC and like Pardon Me Duke

00:06:20.162 --> 00:06:23.198
and people like smaller blogs, Perfection.

00:06:23.198 --> 00:06:24.913
Maybe if they feeling your shit,

00:06:24.913 --> 00:06:26.762
you got a shot, if they put it up,

00:06:26.762 --> 00:06:27.612
there's a way better chance

00:06:27.612 --> 00:06:28.908
that the big blogs'll pick it up.

00:06:28.908 --> 00:06:30.958
Especially after seeing, you know,

00:06:30.958 --> 00:06:32.032
if Perfection picks it up,

00:06:32.032 --> 00:06:33.466
then maybe DC to BC puts it up and

00:06:33.466 --> 00:06:34.694
maybe Pardon Me Duke puts it up.

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:37.786
That is three more smaller blogs

00:06:37.786 --> 00:06:39.747
that still have good followings

00:06:39.747 --> 00:06:40.580
that are putting your shit up

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.072
so the bigger blogs like a
2DopeBoyz might pick it up now.

00:06:43.072 --> 00:06:44.466
And then after they pick it up now...

00:06:44.466 --> 00:06:45.310
So that's the best way.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:48.749
Just start, have big dream
and then just start small,

00:06:48.749 --> 00:06:51.408
But the internet is not
the end all, be all, man.

00:06:51.408 --> 00:06:52.627
It's a lot more to go.

00:06:52.627 --> 00:06:56.534
- Many entrepreneurs
fail due to over funding.

00:06:56.534 --> 00:06:58.427
So you look, we're in
a beautiful location,

00:06:58.427 --> 00:07:01.217
Trattoria el Mulino,
it's a legendary family

00:07:01.217 --> 00:07:03.408
in the restauranteur business

00:07:03.408 --> 00:07:04.834
and they've been doing this for years.

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:08.001
But if you look at somebody
that decides that they can cook

00:07:08.001 --> 00:07:10.303
and they want to work on
grandma's recipe, they'll go out

00:07:10.303 --> 00:07:12.168
and they'll get a hundred
thousand dollar loan,

00:07:12.168 --> 00:07:13.330
they'll open up a restaurant,

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.452
they have no experience doing that,

00:07:14.452 --> 00:07:16.676
they'll have a beautiful
place, great staff,

00:07:16.676 --> 00:07:18.799
but they didn't sell not one piece of food

00:07:18.799 --> 00:07:20.040
in their entire life

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.019
and they didn't understand
the operation of the business.

00:07:22.019 --> 00:07:24.006
Eight months in, a year
in when they realize

00:07:24.006 --> 00:07:25.716
why they don't have any customers,

00:07:25.716 --> 00:07:27.774
because they didn't have a
customer base in the beginning.

00:07:27.774 --> 00:07:29.287
They have a hundred
thousand dollar loan now

00:07:29.287 --> 00:07:31.163
on the business and they haven't
figured out the business.

00:07:31.163 --> 00:07:33.321
Then all of a sudden,
they have to close down.

00:07:33.321 --> 00:07:36.381
I started off literally
with $800 worth of hats,

00:07:36.381 --> 00:07:38.243
and that was the beginning.

00:07:38.243 --> 00:07:39.693
- [Azim] What would be
my advice to students

00:07:39.693 --> 00:07:41.730
who want to start an
organization like Wipro?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.563
- Yes, sir.

00:07:42.563 --> 00:07:44.701
- You know the reality is
you'll have to start small.

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:46.534
Like we started small.

00:07:47.757 --> 00:07:50.822
You must have a very clear understanding

00:07:50.822 --> 00:07:53.253
of why you want to do it,

00:07:53.253 --> 00:07:56.289
and what focus you want to build.

00:07:56.289 --> 00:07:57.568
And the focus you want to build

00:07:57.568 --> 00:07:59.949
in terms of starting an organization,

00:07:59.949 --> 00:08:03.104
is something that must be
deeply passionate inside.

00:08:03.104 --> 00:08:05.207
Because you're going to
go through ups and downs.

00:08:05.207 --> 00:08:07.748
In many cases you're going to fail.

00:08:07.748 --> 00:08:10.335
Certainly in parts of your journey

00:08:10.335 --> 00:08:12.914
you're going to have major failures.

00:08:12.914 --> 00:08:15.622
So unless you have a very clear commitment

00:08:15.622 --> 00:08:17.509
to the focus which you build in terms of

00:08:17.509 --> 00:08:19.749
what you want to build successfully,

00:08:19.749 --> 00:08:22.774
and have the flexibility
to change that focus

00:08:22.774 --> 00:08:25.779
because you've not judged
the market properly.

00:08:25.779 --> 00:08:27.486
Markets don't run after you, you know.

00:08:27.486 --> 00:08:29.915
You have to run after
what the market demand is,

00:08:29.915 --> 00:08:32.686
what the market demand you can create.

00:08:32.686 --> 00:08:35.015
But you have to be persistent

00:08:35.015 --> 00:08:37.662
and you have to be
prepared to make sacrifices

00:08:37.662 --> 00:08:39.755
because you will have to make sacrifices

00:08:39.755 --> 00:08:43.177
in the early stages, and
some very major sacrifices.

00:08:43.177 --> 00:08:46.162
And most of them will
be financial sacrifices.

00:08:46.162 --> 00:08:47.395
Because you won't get cash flows

00:08:47.395 --> 00:08:49.495
the way you hoped to get cash flows.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:52.026
Unless you have a brilliant, genius idea.

00:08:52.026 --> 00:08:53.614
Then you'll get cash flows.

